# The other half of ADR-0401's count, and the one that is a fact about how
# ADR-0396 stores a document rather than about dirtiness.
#
# `ed.doc` is the document being edited and `ed.bank[ed.cur]` is a *stale
# copy* of it: `EditGo` writes the live one back only as it moves away, so
# the slot the cursor is in holds whatever that document looked like the last
# time it was left. `EditDirtyCount` therefore skips it, exactly as `EditFind`
# does and for the same reason.
#
# This session comes back to where it started, which is the only way to make
# that slot hold something: `a.pas` is typed into, left for `b.pas`, and
# returned to. It ends with two documents holding changes and one of them
# under the cursor -- so a count that read the bank without skipping the
# current slot would see `a.pas` twice and answer 3.
name a.pas
size 10 30
push program a(output);
keys X
draw
func 3
keys b.pas
ctrl M
push program b(output);
keys Y
draw
func 6
draw
